{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use existing build system (Maven/Gradle) for Kafka dependency upgrade.",
    "Load generators will be implemented as standalone Java applications using the same tech stack as Spring XD.",
    "Benchmarks will be executed on identical hardware to ensure comparability between Kafka 0.8.1 and 0.8.2.",
    "Documentation (Kryo guidelines, benchmark results, design proposal) will be authored in Markdown for easy publishing.",
    "Stateful stream processing design will leverage Spring XD's existing architecture and consider Kafka Streams concepts for native integration."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Developer has full access to the Spring XD codebase and necessary infrastructure (Kafka clusters, benchmark hardware).",
    "Kafka 0.8.2 is largely compatible with the current Spring XD version; only minor API adjustments are required.",
    "The Tuple class is well-encapsulated, limiting the scope of refactoring to a few modules.",
    "Kryo serialization is already in use; optimization guidelines focus on configuration tuning rather than new implementation.",
    "Benchmark environment can be provisioned with both Kafka versions (either concurrently or sequentially).",
    "The blog post targets external audience and requires polished writing and formatting.",
    "The stateful stream processing study (U8) is a design exploration only; no implementation is expected in this increment.",
    "All performance tests are automated and can be run repeatedly with minimal manual intervention."
  ],
